 "note": "Add a board by appending {ats, slug, name, tags?}. ats is greenhouse, lever or ashby. Workday entries need tenant, wd (wd1/wd5), site. tags may include ai, nonprofit, maternal; the scanner adds a score bonus for ai and nonprofit. Added 2026-09-20 from the Lumira health AI funding recap: Ferry Health, Tandem Health, Archy, Ez Health, Epsilon Health, H1 (Defacto Health was acquired by H1 on 2026-09-09, so its roles surface there), Verily on Workday. Assort Health was already tracked. Nara Health (narabenefits.com) and Graph AI (graphsafety.ai) publish no scannable board; Implicity uses Welcome to the Jungle, which the scanner cannot read, and its two US roles are York-based. A board or Workday entry with \"watch\": true is a watched employer: its remote-US roles that match a title family are listed even when the focus block would drop them (full-time, for-profit) and however old the posting is; they carry a \"Watched employer\" badge."
